Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 22:37:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cpuinfo-overlay): correct Tensor-G2 profile, persistent
 Serial (CLO-114)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug: cpuinfo.spoofed had wrong CPU part codes (4×0xd42 A78AE + 4×0xd05),
BogoMIPS=2.00 (implausible), and Serial derived from boot_id (rotates every
container restart — detectable as fingerprint instability).

Fix:
- cpuinfo.spoofed: real Tensor-G2 (2,2,4) topology — 2×0xd44 X1 (variant 0x1),
  2×0xd41 A78 (variant 0x1), 4×0xd05 A55 (variant 0x2). BogoMIPS=38.40 from
  Pixel-7 Pro reference dump. Features line includes ssbs.
- service.sh: Serial now derived once from container UUID (hostname →
  /etc/machine-id → /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid), sha256[:16], written to
  /data/local/tmp/cpuinfo-overlay.serial (chmod 0400), read on all subsequent
  boots. Eliminates per-boot rotation.
- tests/profile-check.sh (new): acceptance gate — verifies topology, BogoMIPS
  in [30,60], and Serial stability across two consecutive invocations.

Acceptance gate:
  bash agents/stability/stack/modules/cpuinfo-overlay/tests/profile-check.sh
  PASS: 8 processors, parts d44,d44,d41,d41,d05,d05,d05,d05; BogoMIPS in [30,60]; Serial=d83ad185db8ba12f stable
  EXIT=0 (two consecutive runs, same Serial both times)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
